WEBVTT


00:01:39.722 --> 00:01:41.246
Ladies and gentlemen...


00:01:41.424 --> 00:01:43.415
...we are beginning our descent
into Berlin Tegel...


00:01:43.593 --> 00:01:47.723
...where local time is 8:30 a.m. And the
temperature is a cool minus four degrees.


00:01:47.897 --> 00:01:49.023
Morning.


00:01:49.866 --> 00:01:51.333
Did you sleep?


00:01:51.501 --> 00:01:54.470
No. I'll sleep at the hotel.


00:01:55.605 --> 00:01:56.902
You'll do great.


00:01:58.641 --> 00:02:00.233
You always do.


00:02:14.657 --> 00:02:16.181
What's the purpose of your visit?


00:02:16.359 --> 00:02:20.193
We're here for a biotechnology summit.
I'm giving a presentation.


00:02:25.201 --> 00:02:28.466
Mr. And Mrs. Harris, welcome to Berlin.


00:02:28.638 --> 00:02:30.333
Danke schon.


00:02:31.774 --> 00:02:33.503
Next, please.


00:02:34.310 --> 00:02:36.073
"I'm giving a presentation"?


00:02:36.245 --> 00:02:38.611
Well, she asked.


00:02:42.018 --> 00:02:44.885
- Oof. Welcome to Berlin.
- Taxi.


00:02:45.054 --> 00:02:46.715
Taxi.


00:03:07.210 --> 00:03:09.576
Martin, get in the car. Let him do that.


00:03:13.616 --> 00:03:14.640
Oh, ya-ya.


00:03:51.487 --> 00:03:52.954
What do you think he's saying?


00:03:53.556 --> 00:03:54.955
No idea.


00:04:01.397 --> 00:04:03.888
Look. Isabel Kronenberger is showing
here on Saturday.


00:04:04.067 --> 00:04:05.227
Oh, yeah.


00:04:05.401 --> 00:04:07.926
Remember when we saw her
in Chicago?


00:04:08.137 --> 00:04:09.900
Yes.


00:04:12.408 --> 00:04:17.505
Why don't I meet you there on Saturday
after my lunch with Professor Bressler?


00:04:17.680 --> 00:04:19.375
Yeah.


00:04:20.149 --> 00:04:21.241
If you promise.


00:04:21.417 --> 00:04:22.941
I promise.


00:04:57.587 --> 00:05:00.112
- Welcome to the Hotel Adlon Kempinski.
- Thank you.


00:05:00.289 --> 00:05:02.587
You check in, honey.
I'll take care of this.


00:05:02.758 --> 00:05:04.225
Have you stayed with us before?


00:05:04.393 --> 00:05:06.588
- First time in Berlin.
- First time in Berlin.


00:05:09.999 --> 00:05:12.695
If there's anything else I can do for you...


00:05:12.869 --> 00:05:14.131
How much do I owe you?


00:05:14.303 --> 00:05:15.395
Thirty-seven, sir.


00:05:15.838 --> 00:05:18.830
Welcome to the Adlon Kempinski Berlin.
How may I help you, madam?


00:05:19.008 --> 00:05:22.136
- Dr. And Mrs. Harris, the Eisenhower suite.
- Of course.


00:05:22.879 --> 00:05:25.143
- Wait, wait.
- Everything okay, sir?


00:05:25.314 --> 00:05:28.112
- Is this everything from the taxi?
- Yes, sir.


00:05:30.486 --> 00:05:34.422
I'm afraid, Mrs. Harris, but the Eisenhower
suite may not be available right now.


00:05:34.590 --> 00:05:35.989
What do you mean "not available"?


00:05:36.159 --> 00:05:37.751
There have been changes,
security reasons.


00:05:39.128 --> 00:05:40.823
But we confirmed two weeks ago.


00:05:40.997 --> 00:05:42.862
Would you allow me
to answer the phone?


00:05:43.032 --> 00:05:45.023
I'll go to the airport. I'll be back, okay?


00:06:16.299 --> 00:06:17.994
Oh, please.


00:06:18.167 --> 00:06:20.431
Excuse me, driver?
Is there another route?


00:06:36.652 --> 00:06:37.676
Oh, come on.


00:06:54.136 --> 00:06:55.330
- Look out!
- No!


00:08:18.854 --> 00:08:21.584
Hello? Hello?


00:08:22.792 --> 00:08:23.918
Can you hear me?


00:10:05.027 --> 00:10:07.018
Dr. Farge?


00:10:09.198 --> 00:10:12.599
Dr. Farge. Dr. Farge.


00:10:25.448 --> 00:10:27.746
I don't speak German.


00:10:28.017 --> 00:10:29.848
Are you English?


00:10:30.786 --> 00:10:32.253
American.


00:10:34.557 --> 00:10:36.787
You have been in an accident.


00:10:36.959 --> 00:10:38.620
Accident?


00:10:41.063 --> 00:10:43.190
Can you tell me your name?


00:10:45.267 --> 00:10:46.461
Your name.


00:10:46.635 --> 00:10:50.093
Martin. Martin Harris.


00:10:51.073 --> 00:10:53.234
Dr. Martin Harris.


00:10:54.944 --> 00:10:56.070
Where's my wife, Liz?


00:10:58.681 --> 00:11:01.081
- Is she hurt? Is she hurt? Where is she?
- Calm down.


00:11:01.250 --> 00:11:04.413
It's all right, Dr. Harris.
You were the only passenger.


00:11:04.587 --> 00:11:07.112
The taxi you were in went into the river.


00:11:07.289 --> 00:11:09.951
Your heart stopped for several minutes.


00:11:10.259 --> 00:11:14.593
It's Thursday, November 24th.
You have been in a coma for four days.


00:11:14.763 --> 00:11:19.791
Thanksgiving.
But my wife, she's in Berlin with me.


00:11:19.969 --> 00:11:21.994
Where is she? Why isn't she here?


00:11:22.171 --> 00:11:25.572
We couldn't find any identification
with you, Dr. Harris.


00:11:26.408 --> 00:11:27.773
No, no, no.


00:11:27.943 --> 00:11:29.604
- Please, calm down.
- Aah.


00:11:29.812 --> 00:11:33.407
Where can we reach your wife?
Does she have a cell phone?


00:11:33.582 --> 00:11:36.016
Of course she has a cell phone. It's...


00:11:39.722 --> 00:11:40.950
Uh...


00:11:43.225 --> 00:11:44.317
I can't remember.


00:11:44.493 --> 00:11:48.361
Can you tell me what you do remember,
Martin?


00:11:49.498 --> 00:11:52.194
Bits and pieces. Arriving at the airport.


00:11:53.235 --> 00:11:55.726
Getting in a taxi with Liz...


00:11:56.972 --> 00:11:58.906
...but I don't know how I got here.


00:11:59.108 --> 00:12:02.202
There are no rules with severe trauma
of this kind.


00:12:02.378 --> 00:12:04.312
Memories get lost or fractured.


00:12:04.480 --> 00:12:06.641
Most of them return,
although it's unlikely...


00:12:06.815 --> 00:12:10.148
...you will ever fully recall the events
around your accident.


00:12:10.319 --> 00:12:13.117
In the meantime, let us see
if anyone has filed a report...


00:12:13.289 --> 00:12:15.018
...looking for a Martin Harris, okay?


00:12:15.190 --> 00:12:17.658
- Yes, yes, yes.
- Okay.


00:12:26.001 --> 00:12:28.401
From London
with Kevin Spencer and Diana Bailey.


00:12:28.571 --> 00:12:30.562
Good evening.
Welcome to the BNI World News.


00:12:30.739 --> 00:12:32.297
Here are today's top stories.


00:12:32.474 --> 00:12:33.498
The Prime Mini...


00:12:34.877 --> 00:12:36.469
Clothes. For you.


00:12:37.880 --> 00:12:40.872
Has anybody been
looking for me? My wife?


00:12:41.884 --> 00:12:42.976
Meine Frau?


00:13:16.118 --> 00:13:17.380
Come here, you.


00:13:23.392 --> 00:13:25.383
It's beautiful. Just beautiful.


00:13:25.561 --> 00:13:27.222
I'm glad you like it.


00:13:32.234 --> 00:13:34.259
She gave it to me as a gift.


00:13:34.670 --> 00:13:37.503
In Paris. On our honeymoon.


00:14:17.980 --> 00:14:22.917
Prince Shada arrived in Berlin today for
this year's biotechnology global summit.


00:14:23.085 --> 00:14:25.451
The personal attendance
of the flamboyant prince...


00:14:25.621 --> 00:14:29.148
...has fueled speculation that the summit,
now in its 10th year...


00:14:29.324 --> 00:14:32.691
...will witness the announcement
of a major scientific breakthrough.


00:14:32.861 --> 00:14:35.125
With the world's leading researchers
convening...


00:14:35.297 --> 00:14:37.731
...at the luxurious Hotel Adlon
in Central Berlin...


00:14:37.900 --> 00:14:40.027
- Hotel Adlon.
...the field of biotechnology...


00:14:40.202 --> 00:14:42.864
...steps into the forefront
of the media spotlight.


00:14:43.038 --> 00:14:44.767
I'm here for the summit.


00:14:44.940 --> 00:14:45.998
Nurse.


00:14:46.542 --> 00:14:48.373
You have to realize the risk.


00:14:48.544 --> 00:14:51.012
Doctor, I've been gone for four days.


00:14:51.180 --> 00:14:54.377
My wife is out there in a city
she doesn't know. She'll be terrified.


00:14:54.550 --> 00:14:56.677
I need to find her.


00:14:59.555 --> 00:15:00.681
Sign this.


00:15:01.523 --> 00:15:04.048
It releases you from my care.


00:15:05.027 --> 00:15:06.324
And here's my card.


00:15:07.663 --> 00:15:11.622
Any nausea, dizziness, difficulty with
speech, you contact me immediately.


00:15:11.800 --> 00:15:13.427
- Do you understand?
- Thank you.


00:15:28.117 --> 00:15:30.779
Welcome to the Hotel Adlon Kempinski.
How may I help you?


00:15:30.953 --> 00:15:34.548
Yes, hi. I'm a guest of the hotel.
I lost my room key. I need a new one.


00:15:34.723 --> 00:15:37.157
- What room are you staying in?
- The Eisenhower suite.


00:15:37.326 --> 00:15:40.489
- And may I have your name?
- Martin Harris. Dr. Martin Harris.


00:15:42.064 --> 00:15:44.692
And may I please see some ID,
Mr. Harris?


00:15:44.867 --> 00:15:48.564
There's been a situation.
I've lost my passport.


00:15:49.004 --> 00:15:50.995
I'm going to need some ID, sir.


00:15:51.173 --> 00:15:54.301
If you get someone to escort me
to my room, I can prove it.


00:15:54.476 --> 00:15:56.205
Just give me a moment.


00:16:20.102 --> 00:16:22.070
- Excuse me. Do you have an invitation?
- No.


00:16:22.237 --> 00:16:26.071
I mean, yes. My name is Dr. Martin Harris.
I'm on the list.


00:16:26.241 --> 00:16:28.402
- Let me check.
- I saw my wife go inside.


00:16:28.577 --> 00:16:29.942
I'm trying to find her.


00:16:30.112 --> 00:16:32.137
Herr Strauss?


00:16:34.383 --> 00:16:36.248
- Dr. Martin Harris?
- Yes.


00:16:36.885 --> 00:16:41.447
Yes. There you are. I'm Herr Strauss,
head of the Hotel Security.


00:16:41.623 --> 00:16:45.389
Do you have any identification?
Passport, driver's license?


00:16:45.561 --> 00:16:47.495
No, I don't, but...


00:16:47.963 --> 00:16:50.955
- You would know him, he's over there.
- Professor Bressler!


00:16:51.133 --> 00:16:53.101
- Professor Bressler!
- Sir, please.


00:16:53.268 --> 00:16:54.929
He knows me.
He can confirm who I am.


00:16:55.103 --> 00:16:59.733
- Lf you will be patient, sir, no problem.
- I'm being very patient.


00:17:01.210 --> 00:17:05.408
Thank God. There she is. That's my wife,
over there by the buffet table.


00:17:09.151 --> 00:17:13.144
I have been missing for four days and she
has no idea what happened to me...


00:17:13.322 --> 00:17:15.916
...so I need you to take me to her
right now.


00:17:21.730 --> 00:17:24.255
- Okay.
- Thank you.


00:17:25.868 --> 00:17:28.701
- The lady in the dark dress.
- Okay.


00:17:31.373 --> 00:17:32.772
Excuse me, madam.


00:17:34.910 --> 00:17:36.400
Your husband is here.


00:17:37.613 --> 00:17:41.014
Liz. Oh, Jesus.


00:17:41.450 --> 00:17:44.681
Excuse me. Do I know you?


00:17:48.857 --> 00:17:51.155
But, Liz... What's wrong?


00:17:51.727 --> 00:17:52.955
I'm sorry.


00:17:53.128 --> 00:17:57.497
I was in an accident. I was in a coma.
They didn't know who I was.


00:18:01.003 --> 00:18:02.334
I said I'm sorry.


00:18:03.772 --> 00:18:06.707
Oh, you must have me confused
with someone else.


00:18:08.043 --> 00:18:09.408
Liz.


00:18:10.245 --> 00:18:12.907
It's me, Martin.


00:18:13.282 --> 00:18:14.510
Your husband.


00:18:17.753 --> 00:18:20.278
This is a misunderstanding.
I don't know this man.


00:18:21.023 --> 00:18:22.650
- Okay.
- Martin.


00:18:24.026 --> 00:18:26.085
This is my husband.


00:18:26.261 --> 00:18:28.354
You are Dr. Martin Harris?


00:18:28.530 --> 00:18:29.656
Last time I looked.


00:18:31.066 --> 00:18:32.158
Yep, still me.


00:18:35.370 --> 00:18:38.203
What's going on here?
Is this some kind of a joke?


00:18:39.141 --> 00:18:40.506
Joke about what?


00:18:41.076 --> 00:18:43.306
Because it's not very funny.


00:18:43.478 --> 00:18:45.708
- Do you know this man?
- No.


00:18:46.782 --> 00:18:48.409
Who the hell are you?


00:18:49.785 --> 00:18:51.343
Who the hell are you?


00:18:53.121 --> 00:18:54.645
I'm her husband.


00:18:55.824 --> 00:18:57.519
Okay. Okay.


00:18:57.693 --> 00:19:01.094
Would you mind just getting him
away from us, please?


00:19:01.496 --> 00:19:03.020
- Liz. Liz, stop this.
- Hey.


00:19:03.198 --> 00:19:05.962
- Gentlemen, please, please, please.
- Get your hands off me.


00:19:06.134 --> 00:19:07.567
- Back off.
- What's going on?


00:19:07.736 --> 00:19:08.828
- Tell me.
- Back off!


00:19:09.004 --> 00:19:11.336
- What's this all about?
- Why don't you take a walk?


00:19:11.506 --> 00:19:12.905
Gentlemen, please.


00:19:13.075 --> 00:19:14.906
- Don't touch me.
- Come on, come on!


00:19:15.110 --> 00:19:17.510
If you don't leave now,
we have to call the police.


00:19:17.679 --> 00:19:20.910
Call the police! Call the goddamn army!
That's a good idea!


00:19:21.083 --> 00:19:23.347
What's happening?
You're embarrassing me. Please.


00:19:23.518 --> 00:19:24.985
- Get him out of here.
- Liz!


00:19:25.153 --> 00:19:28.145
- I must apologize. Have a nice evening.
- I was hurt!


00:19:28.323 --> 00:19:30.951
- Liz! Why are you doing this to me?
- You okay?


00:19:31.126 --> 00:19:32.457
Can you believe this?


00:19:32.761 --> 00:19:33.887
Right there.


00:19:34.062 --> 00:19:36.622
That's Liz. And I am...


00:19:40.068 --> 00:19:43.799
I must've been outside.
I can't remember.


00:19:44.339 --> 00:19:47.638
Well, as you can see, you are not there.


00:19:47.843 --> 00:19:51.244
Immigration confirms the arrival
of a Dr. And Mrs. Harris...


00:19:51.413 --> 00:19:54.644
...on November the 20th at 7:40 a.m.
- Yes.


00:19:54.816 --> 00:19:58.115
At 8:50, she checked into their suite
at the hotel...


00:19:58.286 --> 00:20:01.847
...followed by Dr. Harris
at 3 in the afternoon.


00:20:02.024 --> 00:20:04.151
- What?
- Danke.


00:20:04.926 --> 00:20:08.054
Wait. He's... He's not Martin Harris.


00:20:08.230 --> 00:20:10.994
I am Dr. Martin Harris.


00:20:11.166 --> 00:20:14.329
The man upstairs is pretending
to be me.


00:20:14.503 --> 00:20:16.767
And this impostor,
did he also steal your wife?


00:20:16.938 --> 00:20:19.406
He must be forcing her or something.


00:20:19.574 --> 00:20:22.168
Well, why? Help me. Why?


00:20:22.344 --> 00:20:25.279
For God's sake,
just do an Internet search.


00:20:25.447 --> 00:20:28.245
There are over 400 Martin Harrises
in the United States, sir.


00:20:28.417 --> 00:20:30.180
We already checked.


00:20:30.685 --> 00:20:34.246
Rod. Rodney Cole,
a colleague at Langemore in the States.


00:20:34.423 --> 00:20:36.823
A dear friend.
He can verify who I am.


00:20:36.992 --> 00:20:38.823
Please, call him. It's 001...


00:20:41.797 --> 00:20:45.358
...508-146-2595.


00:20:48.470 --> 00:20:50.734
This is Dr. Cole. I'm having an...


00:20:50.906 --> 00:20:52.271
Sorry, answering machine.


00:20:52.441 --> 00:20:53.533
Please, leave a message.


00:20:53.708 --> 00:20:57.075
Professor Bressler. Talk to him.
He's the reason I'm in Berlin.


00:20:57.245 --> 00:20:59.713
He invited me over to the summit
to discuss my thesis.


00:20:59.881 --> 00:21:01.644
- You know Professor Bressler?
- Yes.


00:21:01.817 --> 00:21:05.776
Well, we haven't actually met,
but we've been speaking on the phone...


00:21:05.954 --> 00:21:07.478
...e- mailing, dozens of times.


00:21:11.226 --> 00:21:13.194
- Why don't you arrest him?
- For what?


00:21:14.029 --> 00:21:15.826
Entering the country legally?


00:21:15.997 --> 00:21:20.457
Presenting all the correct documentation
and sharing a hotel suite with his wife?


00:21:20.635 --> 00:21:22.967
Excuse me. With your wife.


00:21:24.039 --> 00:21:26.667
She is my wife.


00:21:27.375 --> 00:21:30.503
Herr Strauss? I found a Dr. Martin Harris
at Langemore University.


00:21:30.679 --> 00:21:34.115
Yes. Thank you.
That's what I've been trying...


00:21:37.752 --> 00:21:39.242
Okay.


00:21:40.222 --> 00:21:42.349
Wait, please, wait.


00:21:42.524 --> 00:21:46.051
You're going to arrest me?
I demand to speak to my embassy.


00:21:46.228 --> 00:21:49.595
Unfortunately, it's your Thanksgiving.
The embassy's closed until Monday.


00:21:57.038 --> 00:22:00.769
Herr Strauss,
can I have a quiet word, please?


00:22:01.977 --> 00:22:03.376
Okay.


00:22:06.581 --> 00:22:08.048
Listen...


00:22:10.018 --> 00:22:12.680
...you're probably right. L...


00:22:12.988 --> 00:22:14.683
The accident.


00:22:15.390 --> 00:22:16.584
I, uh...


00:22:16.758 --> 00:22:20.250
I haven't been remembering things
very well. I'm confused.


00:22:20.996 --> 00:22:24.261
This is my doctor
at the hospital here in Berlin.


00:22:24.432 --> 00:22:29.335
He warned me that this sort of thing,
this was gonna happen.


00:22:30.272 --> 00:22:33.298
I need to go back there now.


00:22:33.742 --> 00:22:36.176
I'm so embarrassed.


00:22:39.214 --> 00:22:43.617
So now you are saying
that you are not Dr. Martin Harris?


00:22:47.756 --> 00:22:49.417
I don't know.


00:23:17.018 --> 00:23:20.579
Wait, stop. Stop. I've changed my mind.


00:24:34.229 --> 00:24:35.696
- Need passport.
- Please.


00:24:36.765 --> 00:24:38.198
Please?


00:24:38.900 --> 00:24:41.767
Police. Very bad.


00:24:49.844 --> 00:24:51.368
This is Dr. Cole.


00:24:51.546 --> 00:24:54.947
I'm having an out-of-office experience
right now. Please, leave a message.


00:24:56.318 --> 00:24:57.876
Rodney, it's me, Martin.


00:24:58.053 --> 00:25:01.420
Listen, I'm in Berlin
for the summit, but...


00:25:01.589 --> 00:25:04.057
It's Liz. She's...


00:25:04.225 --> 00:25:07.319
l... I don't know what she's doing...


00:25:07.495 --> 00:25:09.520
...and there's another man involved.


00:25:09.698 --> 00:25:12.758
It... She... She...


00:25:14.936 --> 00:25:17.268
I'm in trouble, Rod. We...


00:25:18.807 --> 00:25:20.035
Shit.


00:29:04.532 --> 00:29:06.693
He says he doesn't care
if she saved your life.


00:29:09.437 --> 00:29:12.873
The bitch cost him 20,000 Euros.


00:29:14.475 --> 00:29:18.241
The insurance won't cover the cab
as she had no license.


00:29:20.615 --> 00:29:25.177
He says illegal immigrants
are destroying German society.


00:29:27.555 --> 00:29:29.887
So I'm guessing he doesn't know
where she is.


00:29:30.058 --> 00:29:32.026
No one knows where she is.


00:29:34.829 --> 00:29:38.321
Well, thank him for his time.


00:29:40.835 --> 00:29:41.859
Excuse me.


00:29:42.036 --> 00:29:44.129
Hey, American.
I'm sorry we couldn't help you.


00:29:44.305 --> 00:29:46.000
You know where she is, I can tell.


00:29:46.174 --> 00:29:49.507
Look, I just wanna thank her.
She saved my life.


00:29:49.711 --> 00:29:52.839
I thought maybe I could give her
some money. I just wanna thank her.


00:29:54.549 --> 00:29:56.039
Please.


00:30:11.399 --> 00:30:12.730
You remember me?


00:30:13.267 --> 00:30:15.201
- I was in your taxi.
- I don't drive taxi.


00:30:16.471 --> 00:30:17.802
I was in your taxi.


00:30:17.972 --> 00:30:19.234
We crashed.


00:30:19.407 --> 00:30:21.534
I need to know,
where did you pick me up?


00:30:22.377 --> 00:30:24.242
- Where was I going?
- How did you find me?


00:30:24.412 --> 00:30:25.436
Your friend, Biko.


00:30:28.783 --> 00:30:30.842
Just leave me alone.


00:30:33.087 --> 00:30:34.554
Please, help me.


00:30:35.323 --> 00:30:37.052
Just leave me alone.


00:30:38.893 --> 00:30:40.053
Thank you for saving me.


00:30:53.041 --> 00:30:54.065
Excuse me.


00:30:54.242 --> 00:30:58.144
I need to find Professor Bressler's lab.
I have an appointment at 12:30. I'm late.


00:30:58.312 --> 00:31:01.839
- Your name, please?
- Dr. Martin Harris.


00:31:05.586 --> 00:31:06.848
Wait here, please.


00:31:07.021 --> 00:31:08.352
The professor knows who I am.


00:31:08.523 --> 00:31:10.957
We scheduled this appointment
weeks ago.


00:31:35.116 --> 00:31:36.640
Drake, the English botanist...


00:31:36.818 --> 00:31:39.184
...who wondered how it manages
to reproduce...


00:31:39.353 --> 00:31:42.789
...as it doesn't appear to attract
any insects.


00:31:42.957 --> 00:31:46.859
Yes. One wonders how plants are
developing firm, unlike m...


00:31:51.632 --> 00:31:53.827
- Bressler.
- This lab is restricted. Who are you?


00:31:54.001 --> 00:31:58.131
This man is not Martin Harris.
I am Dr. Martin Harris.


00:31:59.607 --> 00:32:03.509
So, what is this?
There are two Martin Harrises, huh?


00:32:03.678 --> 00:32:05.077
No, let me explain.


00:32:05.246 --> 00:32:08.340
This man showed up at my hotel last night
claiming to be me.


00:32:08.516 --> 00:32:11.485
- The police were called.
- I called the police, son of a bitch!


00:32:11.652 --> 00:32:13.381
He checked himself out of a hospital.


00:32:13.554 --> 00:32:15.146
- He was in an accident.
- Professor.


00:32:17.558 --> 00:32:18.820
Ja. Danke.


00:32:19.393 --> 00:32:21.588
We talked, you and I, on the phone.


00:32:21.763 --> 00:32:24.197
We discussed
alternative forms of propagation.


00:32:24.365 --> 00:32:28.859
I told you about my father,
a schoolteacher, his passion for science.


00:32:29.437 --> 00:32:30.927
We talked about your children...


00:32:31.105 --> 00:32:34.370
...about how much time you've spent
with them since you lost your wife.


00:32:34.542 --> 00:32:36.908
Two girls, right?


00:32:37.078 --> 00:32:40.047
You told me their names. And I...


00:32:40.214 --> 00:32:41.875
I just can't...


00:32:42.350 --> 00:32:44.045
I know them. I know them.


00:32:44.819 --> 00:32:46.844
- Laurel.
- Laurel, Lily, twins.


00:32:47.021 --> 00:32:48.750
Ten years old.


00:32:48.923 --> 00:32:53.019
About the same age I was when I told
my father I wanted to be a botanist.


00:32:53.194 --> 00:32:56.129
Do you remember, Professor?
We talked about that on the phone...


00:32:56.297 --> 00:32:58.458
...how I'd never seen my father
this happy.


00:32:58.633 --> 00:32:59.691
No, that wasn't you.


00:32:59.867 --> 00:33:03.098
Don't you remember? We spoke
about how brave our wives were...


00:33:03.271 --> 00:33:04.465
To marry scientists.


00:33:04.639 --> 00:33:07.267
- I told you about our...
- Our honeymoon in Paris.


00:33:07.475 --> 00:33:10.876
My wife and I. And how she wanted to visit
all the museums.


00:33:11.045 --> 00:33:14.139
- All I wanted to do was go to the...
- L'Ecole Polytechnique.


00:33:14.315 --> 00:33:18.718
But she insisted. And that's how
I first saw Leonardo's Vitruvian man.


00:33:19.387 --> 00:33:20.752
Wow.


00:33:25.593 --> 00:33:26.685
This is not happening.


00:33:28.296 --> 00:33:29.388
Moment, Moment.


00:33:29.564 --> 00:33:34.160
I don't know who this man is,
but he has taken everything from me.


00:33:34.802 --> 00:33:36.997
You have to arrest him.


00:33:37.405 --> 00:33:38.804
Go on, arrest him.


00:33:40.942 --> 00:33:43.672
I don't believe I need to do this.


00:34:16.344 --> 00:34:17.572
No.


00:34:38.132 --> 00:34:41.727
My friend, he...


00:34:42.904 --> 00:34:44.531
...looks...


00:34:45.306 --> 00:34:48.173
No, he finds people.


00:34:53.981 --> 00:34:55.505
Martin.


00:34:56.450 --> 00:34:59.351
The mistake was mine.
I should never have let you leave.


00:34:59.520 --> 00:35:02.182
- What's happening to me, doctor?
- Confusion...


00:35:02.356 --> 00:35:05.792
...memory loss,
complete or partial loss of identity.


00:35:05.960 --> 00:35:08.690
These are common stages in recovery.


00:35:08.863 --> 00:35:10.558
A person can awaken from a coma...


00:35:10.731 --> 00:35:14.690
...convinced of a reality
that was previously only fantasy.


00:35:14.869 --> 00:35:16.928
We are going to sedate you now...


00:35:17.104 --> 00:35:21.063
...do another MRI,
try to find out what's going on, okay?


00:35:21.275 --> 00:35:25.473
If I'm not Martin Harris,
why do I know so much about him?


00:35:26.514 --> 00:35:31.542
Perhaps he was someone
you read about...


00:35:31.719 --> 00:35:33.209
...or met once in passing.


00:35:34.822 --> 00:35:38.280
Do you know what it feels like
to become insane, doctor?


00:35:39.694 --> 00:35:43.960
It's like a war
between being told who you are...


00:35:44.565 --> 00:35:46.760
...and knowing who you are.


00:35:48.102 --> 00:35:50.536
Which do you think wins?


00:36:59.306 --> 00:37:02.275
Hello, Martin. This won't take very long.


00:40:48.902 --> 00:40:52.963
It's okay. I'm feeling much, much better.


00:42:15.923 --> 00:42:19.154
And now with us,
Rebecca for the weather.


00:42:21.395 --> 00:42:22.828
Hello?


00:42:24.932 --> 00:42:26.399
Hello?


00:42:28.502 --> 00:42:30.094
Hello?


00:42:34.641 --> 00:42:37.610
So it's going to be
a cold night here in Central Berlin...


00:42:37.778 --> 00:42:39.575
...with an overnight low
of three degrees...


00:42:39.747 --> 00:42:42.944
...and a high probability of more snow
throughout tomorrow.


00:42:43.150 --> 00:42:45.345
And now to the West,
to the Ruhr Valley.


00:43:11.078 --> 00:43:13.546
- Herr Jurgen?
- Yeah?


00:43:20.687 --> 00:43:21.711
You met her?


00:43:22.322 --> 00:43:24.256
She looked after me in the hospital.


00:43:24.425 --> 00:43:26.620
She was kind to me too.


00:43:27.494 --> 00:43:29.928
I'm sorry. She's dead.


00:43:33.300 --> 00:43:35.598
Come. Come in.


00:43:36.336 --> 00:43:37.826
Thank you.


00:43:49.583 --> 00:43:50.709
Drink?


00:43:50.884 --> 00:43:52.784
No, thanks.


00:43:56.790 --> 00:43:59.122
I was a former member of the Stasi...


00:43:59.993 --> 00:44:02.291
...the Ministry for State Security.


00:44:02.463 --> 00:44:06.559
- East German secret police, huh?
- Yes.


00:44:06.733 --> 00:44:08.564
Proudly.


00:44:18.011 --> 00:44:19.342
Excuse me.


00:44:19.880 --> 00:44:23.043
I cannot drink any longer,
but I like to forget that.


00:44:23.250 --> 00:44:26.447
We Germans are experts at forgetting.
We forgot we were Nazis.


00:44:26.620 --> 00:44:30.989
Now we have forgotten 40 years
of Communism, all gone.


00:44:31.325 --> 00:44:34.920
But it's not just history that's forgotten,
it's people too.


00:44:35.562 --> 00:44:41.262
Please tell me more about
Nurse Gretchen Herfort.


00:44:46.306 --> 00:44:47.830
Quite a story.


00:44:48.008 --> 00:44:51.136
For a moment,
they had me convinced I was crazy.


00:44:51.311 --> 00:44:53.973
But when they came to take me,
when they...


00:44:55.215 --> 00:44:58.810
...killed your friend, I knew.


00:45:00.320 --> 00:45:02.811
I'm not sure how I can be of service.


00:45:02.990 --> 00:45:07.427
I need you to help me prove I'm me.


00:45:10.330 --> 00:45:11.354
May I?


00:45:11.532 --> 00:45:13.397
Please.


00:45:13.567 --> 00:45:15.933
It's a gift from my father.


00:45:16.937 --> 00:45:19.269
I always have it with me.


00:45:31.518 --> 00:45:33.383
These mean anything to you?


00:45:33.554 --> 00:45:35.954
No. It's my wife's writing.


00:45:36.123 --> 00:45:37.954
So they mean something to her.


00:45:41.895 --> 00:45:45.626
That's my schedule for this week.
I wrote it from memory.


00:45:46.700 --> 00:45:48.565
Your wife's involvement in this.


00:45:48.735 --> 00:45:53.229
There must have been something in
the past, a new friend, an acquaintance?


00:45:53.407 --> 00:45:54.669
No, no, no.


00:45:54.841 --> 00:45:56.399
Unexplained absence?


00:45:56.577 --> 00:46:00.172
No, no. There was nothing.
I would've known.


00:46:00.347 --> 00:46:02.474
Men always like to think.


00:46:02.649 --> 00:46:05.516
It's not Liz. I know her.


00:46:05.686 --> 00:46:07.483
Yet she does not know you.


00:46:07.654 --> 00:46:10.987
Look, whoever's been doing this,
they've been planning it for some time.


00:46:11.158 --> 00:46:15.925
They have passports, credit cards,
family photos, for God's sakes.


00:46:16.096 --> 00:46:18.462
I mean, this takes preparation,
doesn't it?


00:46:18.632 --> 00:46:22.864
They have detailed knowledge of my
research, my relationship with Professor...


00:46:23.036 --> 00:46:26.301
As well as the fact that you were going
to have a random accident...


00:46:26.473 --> 00:46:30.739
...that would allow a stranger
to seamlessly take your place?


00:46:30.911 --> 00:46:34.005
These people may be good,
but they are not God.


00:46:34.181 --> 00:46:36.672
A little confirmation would be nice.


00:46:36.850 --> 00:46:39.785
Somewhere there's proof.
They can't have thought of everything.


00:46:39.953 --> 00:46:44.287
The question is,
why would they want to take your place?


00:46:44.691 --> 00:46:46.818
What could they gain from being you?


00:46:46.994 --> 00:46:50.589
What does your wife gain
by denying you exist?


00:46:53.000 --> 00:46:54.900
Do you believe me?


00:46:55.068 --> 00:46:57.696
In the Stasi, we had a basic principle:


00:46:57.904 --> 00:47:01.931
Ask enough questions and a man who
is lying will eventually change his story...


00:47:02.109 --> 00:47:05.510
...but a man who tells the truth
cannot change his...


00:47:05.679 --> 00:47:07.704
...however unlikely his story sounds.


00:47:07.881 --> 00:47:10.714
- Do you believe me?
- I believe...


00:47:11.351 --> 00:47:13.649
...you are telling the truth, Dr. Harris.


00:47:14.121 --> 00:47:16.681
I'll start by calling your colleague
at Langemore.


00:47:16.857 --> 00:47:20.224
As you say, it's Thanksgiving,
and there's the time difference...


00:47:20.394 --> 00:47:23.454
...so it may take time to make contact.


00:47:23.630 --> 00:47:26.360
Then there is the question of...


00:47:27.300 --> 00:47:28.927
Oh, of money. Of course.


00:47:29.102 --> 00:47:33.095
Unfortunately, yes. Money.


00:47:33.874 --> 00:47:38.538
Of course. Here.
Here's everything I have.


00:47:39.513 --> 00:47:42.243
I'll pay you in full as soon as I can.


00:47:46.019 --> 00:47:48.579
- For expenses.
- Sure.


00:47:48.755 --> 00:47:51.485
I'll need 24 hours.
Call me tomorrow afternoon.


00:47:51.658 --> 00:47:55.788
And go find your taxi driver.
See if she'll talk to me.


00:47:56.229 --> 00:47:59.630
She was there at the beginning of all this.
Perhaps she knows something.


00:47:59.800 --> 00:48:01.427
I've already tried.


00:48:01.868 --> 00:48:04.860
There may be details we've overlooked.


00:48:05.272 --> 00:48:10.039
That's what I was really known for,
details.


00:48:15.882 --> 00:48:17.406
Gina?


00:48:25.792 --> 00:48:28.352
I know why you ran away
from the accident.


00:48:29.062 --> 00:48:30.552
You're an illegal.


00:48:30.764 --> 00:48:33.995
If the police had picked you up,
they would have deported you.


00:48:35.569 --> 00:48:38.538
Look, I want you to have this.


00:48:38.705 --> 00:48:42.334
- What if I don't want it?
- It's worth at least 5000 Euro.


00:48:42.542 --> 00:48:44.874
Feel the weight of it.
Go on. It's the real thing.


00:48:49.116 --> 00:48:50.777
"E.H. To M.H."?


00:48:50.951 --> 00:48:56.253
Elizabeth Harris, my wife, to me, Martin.
Special gift.


00:48:59.559 --> 00:49:01.959
Okay, Martin Harris.
What do you want?


00:49:02.129 --> 00:49:04.063
There's someone
I need you to speak to.


00:49:04.231 --> 00:49:07.496
- I'm not talking to the police.
- He's not the police. I promise you.


00:49:07.667 --> 00:49:10.261
I just need you to tell him
what happened.


00:49:10.437 --> 00:49:13.031
Anything,
everything you can remember.


00:49:14.407 --> 00:49:16.932
And I need a place to crash tonight.


00:49:21.448 --> 00:49:23.006
Please?


00:49:29.756 --> 00:49:33.886
Sentiment,
it's always the first thing to go.


00:49:44.037 --> 00:49:45.265
Brandt.


00:49:48.275 --> 00:49:49.537
Jurgen?


00:49:57.083 --> 00:50:00.450
I picked you up from the Adlon Hotel.
You wanted to go to the airport.


00:50:01.588 --> 00:50:02.782
You were in a hurry.


00:50:02.956 --> 00:50:04.548
That's it?


00:50:04.991 --> 00:50:08.518
But I'd just arrived.
Doesn't make sense.


00:50:08.695 --> 00:50:12.654
She didn't recognize you?
How long have you been married?


00:50:12.833 --> 00:50:14.425
- Five years.
- Five years?


00:50:14.601 --> 00:50:17.092
I know it sounds crazy, but it's true.


00:50:17.270 --> 00:50:18.430
This is it.


00:50:18.972 --> 00:50:20.166
Sorry, no elevator.


00:50:21.508 --> 00:50:24.568
I know, not the Adlon Hotel.


00:50:37.390 --> 00:50:41.759
The walls are made of cardboard,
but it's home.


00:50:42.529 --> 00:50:45.760
I have to work tonight.
You can sleep in there.


00:50:45.932 --> 00:50:47.661
I have extra mattress.


00:50:48.468 --> 00:50:50.129
It's quaint.


00:51:52.565 --> 00:51:54.999
Would you mind if I took a shower?


00:51:55.702 --> 00:51:58.193
You could try. I'm not sure you will fit.


00:51:58.905 --> 00:52:04.400
The light is broken. You need to leave
the door open if you want to see anything.


00:52:19.974 --> 00:52:22.772
- I'm sorry. I just... I'm sorry.
- I give you a place to stay.


00:52:22.944 --> 00:52:25.538
- That does not give you the right to...
- You're right.


00:52:26.214 --> 00:52:28.546
They're good, the drawings.


00:52:42.196 --> 00:52:43.891
You want to know?


00:52:49.103 --> 00:52:50.502
This is me.


00:52:50.672 --> 00:52:53.539
Two thousand
two hundred fifty-eight Euros...


00:52:54.275 --> 00:52:55.742
...and counting.


00:52:56.444 --> 00:53:01.381
I get to 4000, I can buy papers
so I can get the hell out of here.


00:53:02.216 --> 00:53:04.776
Sell the watch.
You'll get more than you need.


00:53:04.952 --> 00:53:06.647
I plan to.


00:53:25.840 --> 00:53:27.034
Ohh.


00:53:27.375 --> 00:53:29.104
How do you sleep?


00:53:29.310 --> 00:53:32.643
Eh. He never goes for very long.


00:53:34.449 --> 00:53:35.882
This guy, Jurgen.


00:53:36.050 --> 00:53:39.178
He's absolutely no danger to you.


00:53:42.423 --> 00:53:43.651
Okay.


00:53:56.571 --> 00:53:57.765
Hello.


00:53:58.973 --> 00:54:00.133
You got company.


00:54:00.308 --> 00:54:01.434
Do you have the keys?


00:54:01.609 --> 00:54:04.169
Bring it back to my place,
leave the keys on the TV...


00:54:04.345 --> 00:54:06.643
...and don't forget to reset the meter.


00:54:06.814 --> 00:54:09.339
- You're the best.
- I know. Come.


00:54:12.920 --> 00:54:15.445
Yes, I sleep with every American
you send my way.


00:54:15.623 --> 00:54:17.250
No need to explain.


00:54:36.644 --> 00:54:38.669
Biko! You're going to be late.


00:56:00.661 --> 00:56:01.685
Shh.


00:56:07.101 --> 00:56:08.591
Jones?


00:56:58.886 --> 00:57:01.286
Biko? Biko?


00:57:55.376 --> 00:57:57.003
Who are you?


00:57:57.812 --> 00:57:59.780
Who the hell are you?


00:58:06.921 --> 00:58:08.149
Biko's keys.


00:58:08.322 --> 00:58:11.382
Give them to me.
Come on, you can't stay here.


00:58:24.105 --> 00:58:25.697
This one!


00:58:39.920 --> 00:58:41.046
Are you all right?


00:58:42.923 --> 00:58:45.721
That guy,
he killed a nurse in the hospital.


00:58:45.893 --> 00:58:48.361
- What?
- He killed a nurse.


00:58:53.468 --> 00:58:54.662
Shit!


00:59:24.932 --> 00:59:27.264
- Left, go left!
- Hang on!


01:00:07.475 --> 01:00:09.204
- Where is he?
- I can't see him.


01:00:20.621 --> 01:00:23.454
- Where is...? Where's the wiper switch?
- It's on the left!


01:00:24.325 --> 01:00:25.724
Shit!


01:00:42.777 --> 01:00:44.404
Come on! Go!


01:01:24.051 --> 01:01:25.882
- Get off the tracks!
- I'm trying to!


01:01:39.834 --> 01:01:41.301
Jesus!


01:02:06.060 --> 01:02:07.357
Come on, come on! Go!


01:02:12.833 --> 01:02:14.130
- Come on!
- Run!


01:02:27.982 --> 01:02:29.108
In here.


01:02:29.517 --> 01:02:32.111
Out of the way. Out of the way.


01:02:34.889 --> 01:02:36.789
- We are being followed.
- Vladimir.


01:03:13.561 --> 01:03:15.688
How does it feel


01:03:17.198 --> 01:03:19.428
To treat me like you do?


01:03:20.534 --> 01:03:23.731
When you've laid your hands upon me


01:03:24.205 --> 01:03:27.140
And you've told me who you are


01:03:28.376 --> 01:03:30.810
I thought I was mistaken


01:03:35.950 --> 01:03:38.180
How do I feel?


01:03:39.153 --> 01:03:42.088
Tell me now how do I feel?


01:03:46.026 --> 01:03:47.653
Gina.


01:03:49.363 --> 01:03:52.890
You have to know I have never laid eyes
on those men.


01:03:54.368 --> 01:03:56.563
Why the hell did you
have to get into my taxi?


01:03:56.737 --> 01:03:58.705
I wish I hadn't. Believe me.


01:04:02.443 --> 01:04:06.504
And Biko. His family is in Africa.


01:04:06.680 --> 01:04:10.116
The money will just stop coming.
They will never know why.


01:04:14.255 --> 01:04:16.314
Men like that, back there.


01:04:16.490 --> 01:04:18.481
I have seen those kind of men before.


01:04:19.660 --> 01:04:21.924
They killed my family in Bosnia.


01:04:22.096 --> 01:04:25.224
My mother, my father, my brothers,
slaughtered!


01:04:25.966 --> 01:04:27.058
We have to disappear.


01:04:27.601 --> 01:04:32.061
- Gina, they're after me, not you.
- Don't be stupid. They're after both of us!


01:04:32.239 --> 01:04:35.072
If they killed Biko,
they'll kill me just as easily.


01:05:44.912 --> 01:05:46.539
Are you ready?


01:05:48.315 --> 01:05:50.249
Don't ask.


01:05:58.959 --> 01:06:00.620
Thank you.


01:06:02.830 --> 01:06:06.994
I'm sorry I brought more trouble
into your life.


01:06:08.369 --> 01:06:11.532
I will try and make up for it. I promise.


01:06:16.544 --> 01:06:17.909
I know.


01:06:19.914 --> 01:06:21.848
I've figured something out.


01:06:26.153 --> 01:06:28.781
It's a simple code.


01:06:29.156 --> 01:06:31.351
The first number refers to a page
in the book...


01:06:31.525 --> 01:06:35.359
...the second to a line on that page,
the third to words on that line.


01:06:35.529 --> 01:06:36.723
What are the words?


01:06:36.897 --> 01:06:38.728
The Latin names of two plant species:


01:06:38.899 --> 01:06:42.198
Calochortus albus
and Umbellularia Californica.


01:06:42.703 --> 01:06:46.571
Fairy Lantern and California Bay,
both common, flowering plants.


01:06:46.740 --> 01:06:48.674
What does it mean?


01:06:48.909 --> 01:06:50.706
That I don't know.


01:06:50.878 --> 01:06:53.904
Not part of your work,
or Professor Bressler's?


01:06:54.081 --> 01:06:55.207
No.


01:06:55.382 --> 01:06:58.647
Tell me, Martin, how close
are Professor Bressler and Prince Shada?


01:06:58.819 --> 01:07:02.311
Very close. The prince is sponsoring
the summit. They're both progressives.


01:07:02.489 --> 01:07:04.787
Bressler wants to end world hunger.


01:07:04.959 --> 01:07:07.655
He's researching new forms
of crop cultivation...


01:07:07.828 --> 01:07:10.228
...offering open access to his data.


01:07:10.397 --> 01:07:12.058
The prince funds his work.


01:07:12.232 --> 01:07:15.759
He knows the world will need food
long after his oil resources are depleted.


01:07:15.936 --> 01:07:18.302
Those agricultural patents
will be worth a fortune.


01:07:18.472 --> 01:07:20.770
But the prince's progressiveness
has cost him.


01:07:20.941 --> 01:07:23.808
Extremists in his own country
hate him...


01:07:23.978 --> 01:07:29.314
...and yet he perseveres his course,
despite multiple attempts on his life.


01:07:29.483 --> 01:07:32.941
There's a cocktail party before Bressler's
speech tonight, is that correct?


01:07:33.120 --> 01:07:34.553
Yes.


01:07:35.255 --> 01:07:38.622
For some, that might be a very good
reason to want to be you.


01:07:39.093 --> 01:07:41.493
Martin Harris with just a few guests...


01:07:41.662 --> 01:07:45.189
...in a confined space
with Prince Shada.


01:07:53.774 --> 01:07:56.971
Jurgen may be right,
but he might not be able to prove it.


01:07:57.144 --> 01:07:58.577
I need to find Liz.


01:07:58.746 --> 01:08:00.771
Oh, Martin, that is not a good idea.


01:08:00.948 --> 01:08:03.746
The people who have her
have been sticking to my schedule.


01:08:03.917 --> 01:08:05.578
I know where she'll be today.


01:08:05.753 --> 01:08:09.587
Someone will be watching her.
What if he's there?


01:08:09.757 --> 01:08:14.592
He won't be. He's me, remember?
He'll be meeting with Bressler.


01:08:58.205 --> 01:09:00.435
- Yeah?
- They just sat down.


01:09:00.607 --> 01:09:03.167
Let me know when they leave. Thanks.


01:09:44.184 --> 01:09:45.742
Okay.


01:09:54.962 --> 01:09:57.328
Please leave a message after the tone.


01:11:43.804 --> 01:11:44.828
Liz.


01:11:46.240 --> 01:11:47.605
What are you doing here?


01:11:48.141 --> 01:11:49.165
Liz. What's happening?


01:11:49.343 --> 01:11:51.538
Are you crazy?
You have to leave me alone.


01:11:51.712 --> 01:11:54.442
Why? You have to tell me why.
Are they making you do this?


01:11:54.615 --> 01:11:58.016
- Are they threatening you?
- How did you find me? Did you follow me?


01:11:58.185 --> 01:11:59.675
When we arrived, you saw the ad.


01:11:59.853 --> 01:12:02.947
You mentioned when we first saw
her show, in Chicago, together.


01:12:03.123 --> 01:12:04.954
Don't you remember?


01:12:22.910 --> 01:12:24.901
- I can't get out.
- Come with me right now.


01:12:25.078 --> 01:12:27.239
No. They'll kill us both.


01:12:27.781 --> 01:12:31.114
I never should have left you.
I never should have gotten into that taxi.


01:12:31.285 --> 01:12:33.082
You don't understand, do you?


01:12:33.654 --> 01:12:37.613
Your briefcase.
It got left behind at the airport.


01:12:37.791 --> 01:12:39.258
That's why you were going back.


01:12:39.426 --> 01:12:41.553
You need to find it.


01:12:42.062 --> 01:12:43.086
Wait for me there.


01:12:43.263 --> 01:12:44.287
Liz, Liz, wait.


01:12:59.980 --> 01:13:01.140
I love you.


01:13:12.559 --> 01:13:14.789
- What did she say?
- Not here.


01:13:15.829 --> 01:13:17.660
Where have you been? Hm?


01:13:27.741 --> 01:13:30.301
I have to go to the airport right away.


01:14:00.207 --> 01:14:01.231
Ja?


01:14:01.408 --> 01:14:03.000
- Is this Ernst Jurgen?
- Yes, it is.


01:14:03.176 --> 01:14:06.873
My name is Rodney Cole.
I received a phone message from you.


01:14:07.047 --> 01:14:10.505
And I received two from Martin as well.
What's the problem?


01:14:12.019 --> 01:14:16.251
Oh, dear. Oh, that's unbelievable.
The poor man.


01:14:16.423 --> 01:14:19.358
Well, listen, here's the good news.
I've just arrived in Berlin.


01:14:19.526 --> 01:14:23.895
Yes, I've been teaching in Leipzig,
at the Hochschule fur Technik.


01:14:24.064 --> 01:14:26.692
I'm sorry, please excuse my German.


01:14:26.867 --> 01:14:29.631
Well, I came up for the last day
to hear Bressler's speech.


01:14:29.803 --> 01:14:31.532
I could come right over.


01:14:31.705 --> 01:14:33.332
No, no, no, it's fine.


01:14:33.507 --> 01:14:37.807
It's no problem at all. It's not far.
I know exactly where you are.


01:14:38.211 --> 01:14:41.180
I look forward to meeting you, Mr. Cole.


01:14:41.348 --> 01:14:44.215
Well, then, I'll see you soon. Bye.


01:14:50.524 --> 01:14:52.617
Rodney Cole?


01:14:54.394 --> 01:14:56.191
Leipzig?


01:15:22.789 --> 01:15:23.847
Herr Jurgen?


01:15:24.024 --> 01:15:25.423
Dr. Cole.


01:15:26.026 --> 01:15:27.721
How do you do?


01:15:28.528 --> 01:15:30.086
Thank you.


01:15:38.238 --> 01:15:39.432
Drink?


01:15:39.606 --> 01:15:43.133
I have a bottle labeled brandy,
which is more than likely hair lacquer...


01:15:43.310 --> 01:15:47.371
...or some vodka my neighbor gave me
after it made her husband go blind.


01:15:47.547 --> 01:15:49.071
No, thank you.


01:15:49.249 --> 01:15:51.740
Maybe some coffee?
I'm making some for myself.


01:15:51.918 --> 01:15:54.182
No, I'm fine. Thank you.


01:16:14.174 --> 01:16:16.335
You were in the military.


01:16:18.011 --> 01:16:20.912
In the Stasi in East Germany.


01:16:21.081 --> 01:16:23.845
Well, my grandson's gonna be
very excited to hear that.


01:16:24.017 --> 01:16:26.349
He loves all this Cold War stuff.


01:16:26.520 --> 01:16:28.545
Oh, look at that.


01:16:28.722 --> 01:16:30.451
What kind of car is that?


01:16:30.624 --> 01:16:33.320
That's a Volga GAZ-24.


01:16:33.627 --> 01:16:37.028
Suspension of a donkey cart
and smelled like a tannery.


01:16:38.398 --> 01:16:41.128
Vanished as quickly as the Wall.


01:16:51.478 --> 01:16:56.472
Oh. This business with Martin
is a hell of a thing. How did he find you?


01:16:56.650 --> 01:16:58.845
Quite by chance, as it happens.


01:16:59.019 --> 01:17:03.149
I would say he was damn lucky.
How can I help?


01:17:03.557 --> 01:17:07.323
Come with us to the authorities.
Help them confirm his identity.


01:17:07.494 --> 01:17:11.260
The authorities?
Oh, Jesus. Is it that bad?


01:17:11.431 --> 01:17:16.459
I mean, a man comes to you with a story.
Why did you take his case?


01:17:17.070 --> 01:17:19.538
Eh. Curiosity.


01:17:21.308 --> 01:17:22.775
Is that all?


01:17:22.943 --> 01:17:28.745
There's not much in this world left
to interest an old spy like me.


01:17:28.915 --> 01:17:31.440
A few questions I still think over.


01:17:32.052 --> 01:17:35.180
One in particular
from when I worked for the Aufklarung...


01:17:35.355 --> 01:17:38.415
...our Foreign Intelligence wing.


01:17:40.293 --> 01:17:44.320
They used to talk about
a European-based assassination unit...


01:17:44.497 --> 01:17:47.523
...called Section 15.


01:17:47.934 --> 01:17:49.902
Freelance, deniable.


01:17:50.070 --> 01:17:52.265
They'd work for whoever would pay.


01:17:52.872 --> 01:17:55.067
Public sector, private sector.


01:17:55.242 --> 01:17:57.972
Second-to-none
in their planning and efficiency.


01:17:58.411 --> 01:18:01.278
What's more, they never failed.


01:18:01.448 --> 01:18:03.848
And I am told
they are still in existence...


01:18:04.017 --> 01:18:07.851
...but that's only rumor, of course.


01:18:10.323 --> 01:18:12.917
You had time after I called you.


01:18:13.093 --> 01:18:14.890
Why didn't you run?


01:18:15.061 --> 01:18:18.929
Where should I run from Section 15,
Mr. Cole?


01:18:19.099 --> 01:18:20.828
I can hardly walk.


01:18:22.135 --> 01:18:27.801
Before we could get Chesterfields,
I smoked 60 machorkas a day.


01:18:28.908 --> 01:18:33.174
Filthy Soviet things.
Killed more Russians than Stalin.


01:18:34.381 --> 01:18:38.408
My doctors assure me
I'll soon be joining their list of casualties.


01:18:38.585 --> 01:18:40.143
I want to know how he found you.


01:18:40.353 --> 01:18:44.153
I want every name,
every source you contacted on his behalf.


01:18:45.258 --> 01:18:47.249
And then what?


01:18:48.261 --> 01:18:50.695
We shake hands and you go away?


01:19:23.163 --> 01:19:25.028
Cyanide.


01:19:25.965 --> 01:19:30.766
You never think you'll have the courage
to use it.


01:19:31.538 --> 01:19:33.438
But you do.


01:19:34.774 --> 01:19:36.071
The best of us do.


01:19:45.852 --> 01:19:50.016
What if he remembers everything?


01:19:50.190 --> 01:19:52.385
What then?


01:20:15.081 --> 01:20:17.549
Wait, wait. Please.


01:20:21.087 --> 01:20:26.684
The combination for the lock is...


01:20:33.199 --> 01:20:34.598
Two eight zero...


01:20:38.471 --> 01:20:39.938
Two eight zero six three five.


01:21:33.660 --> 01:21:35.651
Who am I?


01:21:35.829 --> 01:21:37.456
May I?


01:21:56.049 --> 01:21:59.485
You shouldn't stay here.
It's not safe for you.


01:21:59.652 --> 01:22:00.949
Liz told me to wait here.


01:22:05.024 --> 01:22:06.184
Where are you going?


01:22:09.062 --> 01:22:12.327
You've got your life back.
I'm happy for you.


01:22:12.499 --> 01:22:14.126
Now I need to get on with mine.


01:22:14.300 --> 01:22:15.995
Gina.


01:22:31.584 --> 01:22:33.415
Thank you.


01:22:33.953 --> 01:22:35.318
It's more than I need.


01:22:35.488 --> 01:22:39.185
It's less than you deserve.
For everything you've been through.


01:22:39.359 --> 01:22:40.656
Go on, take it.


01:22:45.331 --> 01:22:47.822
What if she told them
where you were going?


01:22:48.001 --> 01:22:49.298
Liz? She wouldn't.


01:22:49.469 --> 01:22:50.493
How do you know?


01:22:50.670 --> 01:22:54.106
Gina, she's my wife.


01:22:56.509 --> 01:22:58.602
Yes, she is.


01:23:02.382 --> 01:23:03.781
It's too heavy for me.


01:23:40.987 --> 01:23:42.477
Martin.


01:23:42.655 --> 01:23:44.282
Martin.


01:23:44.457 --> 01:23:46.755
Oh, my God, look at you.
How are you doing?


01:23:46.926 --> 01:23:48.393
Rodney? What are you doing here?


01:23:48.561 --> 01:23:51.223
Well, you called me.
Don't you remember?


01:23:51.397 --> 01:23:54.696
You left a message on my machine.
I got on the first plane I could.


01:23:54.867 --> 01:23:58.462
- What have you gotten yourself into?
- I'm sorry to drag you into this, but...


01:23:58.671 --> 01:24:01.799
Don't be. We've been friends
for 15 years.


01:24:01.975 --> 01:24:04.569
I know you'd do the same for me.


01:24:21.794 --> 01:24:23.489
Let me take that for you, huh?


01:25:57.790 --> 01:25:59.519
I've never had this happen before.


01:25:59.692 --> 01:26:02.525
You really think you are Martin Harris,
don't you?


01:26:03.796 --> 01:26:06.026
What the hell, Rod?


01:26:06.899 --> 01:26:08.924
You're my oldest friend.


01:26:09.102 --> 01:26:13.539
You know who I am. It's me.
It's not this other guy. He's not...


01:26:13.706 --> 01:26:16.470
Martin Harris? No, course he's not.


01:26:16.642 --> 01:26:17.939
But, then, neither are you.


01:26:19.378 --> 01:26:22.836
- What?
- There is no Martin Harris.


01:26:23.716 --> 01:26:26.207
He doesn't exist.


01:26:26.719 --> 01:26:27.913
You invented him.


01:26:28.721 --> 01:26:30.086
He's your legend.


01:26:30.256 --> 01:26:34.249
You just made him up as a cover to get
into the conference.


01:26:36.262 --> 01:26:40.460
- You're not making sense. Liz...
- Liz.


01:26:41.768 --> 01:26:43.929
Liz is not your wife.


01:26:47.340 --> 01:26:48.967
You were a professional team.


01:26:49.142 --> 01:26:51.736
No. No, no. This is insane. She...


01:26:51.911 --> 01:26:55.074
Your memories are not real.


01:26:55.248 --> 01:26:58.274
Martin Harris is a fabrication.


01:26:58.451 --> 01:27:02.945
You just invented a life,
and then you filled in the gaps.


01:27:08.995 --> 01:27:11.088
She's right. You're really gone on this.


01:27:11.264 --> 01:27:14.597
She had to go in with a backup.
How do you think she feels?


01:27:17.670 --> 01:27:20.138
They're gonna write
a textbook on you someday.


01:27:20.306 --> 01:27:23.104
And thank you for retrieving the briefcase
from the airport.


01:27:23.276 --> 01:27:27.110
Leaving it there was untidy.


01:27:27.280 --> 01:27:31.080
It was a loose end
that didn't fit in with our plans...


01:27:31.284 --> 01:27:33.946
...and Jurgen figured us out.


01:27:36.022 --> 01:27:38.513
By the way, he's dead.


01:27:39.792 --> 01:27:42.226
And he died very well.


01:27:43.095 --> 01:27:47.156
And I'm afraid that isn't something
I'm gonna be able to say about you.


01:27:48.034 --> 01:27:49.899
I'm sorry.


01:27:50.469 --> 01:27:54.803
I'm really, really sorry.


01:28:00.213 --> 01:28:01.737
Rodney!


01:28:03.649 --> 01:28:05.207
Why are you doing this?


01:28:19.432 --> 01:28:21.332
One year of preparation.


01:28:21.968 --> 01:28:24.459
We did everything we could
to make you come back.


01:28:24.637 --> 01:28:28.164
Do you know how much time
you've wasted? It's Thanksgiving.


01:28:28.341 --> 01:28:30.866
I could've been home with my family,
having dinner...


01:28:31.043 --> 01:28:34.103
...instead of cleaning up your mess
because you bumped your head...


01:28:34.280 --> 01:28:36.248
...and started to believe your cover.


01:28:36.415 --> 01:28:37.905
Tell me...


01:28:39.085 --> 01:28:40.518
...who am I?


01:28:43.389 --> 01:28:47.723
You were a trained assassin,
and you were my best boy.


01:28:49.095 --> 01:28:54.590
And now you're just gonna be
another nameless dead junkie.


01:29:47.653 --> 01:29:48.813
Gina, stay down!


01:30:18.351 --> 01:30:20.785
Gina. Gina.


01:30:55.821 --> 01:30:58.813
No. No.


01:31:30.122 --> 01:31:31.749
"Martin Harris...


01:31:31.924 --> 01:31:37.328
...married to Elizabeth Terman,
July 18, 2006, Martha's Vineyard.


01:31:38.497 --> 01:31:41.933
Father died, September 9, 1987,
of a heart attack."


01:31:42.101 --> 01:31:46.299
I made it up. I made it up
to kill a man I've never met.


01:31:56.315 --> 01:31:59.284
Look, August 27th, the entry stamp.


01:31:59.452 --> 01:32:01.943
You were in Berlin three months ago.


01:32:06.392 --> 01:32:09.520
- Are you ready?
- Almost.


01:32:22.641 --> 01:32:24.074
Ready.


01:32:27.079 --> 01:32:30.480
Who are these people?
They can become anyone.


01:32:30.649 --> 01:32:31.843
They...


01:32:33.219 --> 01:32:34.948
We are killers.


01:32:37.022 --> 01:32:39.115
Prince Shada
is gonna be assassinated tonight.


01:32:39.291 --> 01:32:41.953
There's a bomb in his suite.
I put it there.


01:32:43.529 --> 01:32:45.690
You should've let me drown.


01:32:50.269 --> 01:32:52.863
What matters is what you do now,
Martin.


01:33:08.420 --> 01:33:11.753
Prince Shada,
are you going to stay in Berlin?


01:33:12.858 --> 01:33:15.156
Will you be funding
research at the university?


01:33:15.327 --> 01:33:18.956
Are you interested
in GM crops, Prince Shada?


01:33:19.131 --> 01:33:21.998
How long have you been
working with Professor Bressler?


01:34:02.508 --> 01:34:04.169
We're so honored you could attend.


01:34:04.343 --> 01:34:06.277
The honor is all mine.


01:34:12.885 --> 01:34:14.785
Would you like a drink?
In some circles...


01:34:14.954 --> 01:34:18.856
...my husband is more well-known
for his martinis than his research.


01:34:27.433 --> 01:34:30.800
- Do you have an invitation, sir?
- I don't know if I'm supposed to have...


01:34:30.970 --> 01:34:33.200
...an invitation.
- Leo, please, come in.


01:34:33.372 --> 01:34:35.897
I don't think you need
an invitation to your reception.


01:34:36.075 --> 01:34:37.599
Good to see you.


01:34:37.776 --> 01:34:40.711
So good to see you.
Have you met our host?


01:34:40.913 --> 01:34:43.108
- Not yet.
- Hello.


01:34:43.282 --> 01:34:45.443
Now I can see why
somebody would pretend to be him.


01:34:48.187 --> 01:34:49.620
This way.


01:34:59.832 --> 01:35:01.231
Oh, let me take that.


01:35:01.400 --> 01:35:05.496
- I'd rather hold on to this, if you don't mind.
- Oh, you can trust me, Professor.


01:35:06.739 --> 01:35:07.967
Separation anxiety.


01:35:10.075 --> 01:35:12.202
- Just leave it there, if you could.
- Of course.


01:35:12.378 --> 01:35:13.402
Thank you.


01:35:16.515 --> 01:35:17.607
Danke.


01:35:25.357 --> 01:35:27.291
Come, say hello to my friends.


01:35:28.060 --> 01:35:29.550
Danke schon.


01:35:32.731 --> 01:35:34.961
Oh, excuse me.


01:36:19.378 --> 01:36:20.606
It's you.


01:36:23.148 --> 01:36:24.911
I am not so sure about that.


01:36:25.751 --> 01:36:27.878
Many of my relatives would not agree.


01:36:29.455 --> 01:36:31.116
This way.


01:36:36.328 --> 01:36:37.420
Get your hands off her!


01:36:40.499 --> 01:36:41.796
Okay, I'm coming.


01:37:18.604 --> 01:37:22.267
There's a bomb in the Eisenhower suite.
I put it there three months ago!


01:37:22.441 --> 01:37:24.636
Now you are saying you are
Dr. Martin Harris?


01:37:24.810 --> 01:37:25.902
You're not listening!


01:37:26.078 --> 01:37:28.808
Take me to the room.
I'll show you exactly where it is.


01:37:28.981 --> 01:37:31.779
Up to the room, in the middle of a party
with Prince Shada...


01:37:31.950 --> 01:37:36.080
...and the world's leading scientific minds?
Of course, why didn't you say so before?


01:37:46.331 --> 01:37:50.461
I'm not lying! Pull up the reception
recordings from August 27th of this year.


01:37:50.636 --> 01:37:52.570
Do it now, or many people will die!


01:38:03.348 --> 01:38:06.340
- Excuse me, I'm going to grab my bag.
- Sure.


01:38:13.559 --> 01:38:18.258
Here. Why don't you just wear it?
Like some nerdy accessory?


01:38:18.430 --> 01:38:19.897
Oh.


01:38:21.333 --> 01:38:22.925
Thank you.


01:38:32.311 --> 01:38:35.610
- That's got all your secrets in it, right?
- If you'd like to say so...


01:38:35.781 --> 01:38:38.443
Would you excuse me?
I have to go check on something.


01:38:41.820 --> 01:38:44.880
Stop. Stop. That's it.


01:38:45.224 --> 01:38:48.193
Do you see? Look! Do you see?


01:39:04.676 --> 01:39:06.234
Attention, attention...


01:39:06.411 --> 01:39:09.869
...could all guests leave the hotel
by the front entrance?


01:39:14.820 --> 01:39:17.653
- Shit.
- Attention, attention...


01:39:17.823 --> 01:39:21.589
...could all guests leave the hotel by the
front entrance?


01:39:21.760 --> 01:39:23.091
Find the target. Finish it.


01:39:23.262 --> 01:39:26.060
We got what we came for.
I'm going to take care of the bomb.


01:39:26.832 --> 01:39:29.027
- Forget about it.
- They have my image on file...


01:39:29.201 --> 01:39:30.828
...from when we planted it.
- So?


01:39:31.003 --> 01:39:34.302
I don't want my face connected
to an explosion we no longer need.


01:39:34.473 --> 01:39:35.701
Go!


01:39:45.417 --> 01:39:47.214
Lily, Laurel.


01:39:47.853 --> 01:39:52.187
Bressler's girls. Lily, Laurel.
Flowering plants.


01:39:52.357 --> 01:39:55.258
Calochortus albus
and Umbellularia Californica.


01:39:55.427 --> 01:39:57.054
The code, from the book.


01:39:57.229 --> 01:39:58.287
They're his passwords.


01:40:02.501 --> 01:40:05.163
Bressler's supposedly working
on a new strain of corn.


01:40:05.337 --> 01:40:08.272
One that can grow in any climate.
It's revolutionary.


01:40:08.440 --> 01:40:10.601
If they access his research
and kill him...


01:40:10.776 --> 01:40:13.176
...it could be worth billions
in the wrong hands.


01:40:16.381 --> 01:40:18.076
Laurel! Laurel!


01:40:19.251 --> 01:40:21.913
- Papa!
- Laurel!


01:40:22.087 --> 01:40:24.988
That bomb goes off, it'll look as if
Shada was killed by extremists.


01:40:25.157 --> 01:40:27.625
The prince was never the target.
It's Bressler.


01:40:28.460 --> 01:40:32.294
Listen, listen! You have to tell Strauss,
they're after Bressler!


01:40:32.464 --> 01:40:33.954
Do you understand?


01:40:37.769 --> 01:40:38.827
Go! Go!


01:40:40.238 --> 01:40:43.264
Out of the way! Move! Move!


01:40:46.345 --> 01:40:48.245
- Laurel! Laurel!
- Papa!


01:40:49.915 --> 01:40:52.247
Laurel! Laurel!


01:41:08.367 --> 01:41:10.028
Oh, Laurel.


01:41:11.336 --> 01:41:13.236
Papa!


01:41:15.207 --> 01:41:17.175
She was wandering around,
looking for you.


01:41:17.342 --> 01:41:18.639
- Thank you.
- You're welcome.


01:41:18.810 --> 01:41:20.835
- We have to leave.
- Yes, yes.


01:42:06.425 --> 01:42:08.985
Christ, you really don't
remember anything, do you?


01:42:50.902 --> 01:42:52.233
This'll be at the party...


01:42:52.404 --> 01:42:54.804
...where we'll access Bressler's computer
and steal his files.


01:42:54.973 --> 01:42:56.964
The client wants this clean.


01:42:57.142 --> 01:43:00.236
He wants the material from Bressler's
computer and Bressler dead.


01:43:00.412 --> 01:43:02.039
No one can ever know what happened.


01:43:02.214 --> 01:43:05.308
When the bomb goes off,
it'll appear that Shada was the target...


01:43:05.484 --> 01:43:07.645
...and that Bressler
was collateral damage.


01:43:10.222 --> 01:43:11.849
Looks great.


01:43:16.995 --> 01:43:18.826
Time for the A team?


01:43:46.958 --> 01:43:48.619
I didn't forget everything.


01:43:49.127 --> 01:43:51.652
I remember how to kill you, asshole.


01:46:44.636 --> 01:46:47.867
Less than 24 hours
after the failed assassination attempt...


01:46:48.039 --> 01:46:49.131
...on the Saudi prince...


01:46:49.307 --> 01:46:52.504
...Nobel laureate Professor Leo Bressler
announced the development...


01:46:52.677 --> 01:46:54.668
...of a new strain of corn...


01:46:54.846 --> 01:46:59.180
...fast-growing, self-propagating,
drought-tolerant, and pest-resistant...


01:46:59.384 --> 01:47:03.480
...to be made available worldwide
without patent or copyright costs.


01:47:03.655 --> 01:47:07.557
We have made the genetic map
of this new sustenance available to all.


01:47:07.726 --> 01:47:12.629
It's a gift. It's a gift from Prince Shada
and from science to mankind.


01:47:12.797 --> 01:47:16.289
Humanitarian organizations
applauded the announcement...


01:47:16.468 --> 01:47:19.369
...but agri-business companies
were taken by surprise...


01:47:19.537 --> 01:47:22.472
...and watched as stocks plunged
14 percent.


01:47:22.674 --> 01:47:25.609
This is Annabelle Mandeng reporting
from Berlin.


01:47:25.777 --> 01:47:29.304
And in other news, the European
Parliament today passed legislation...


01:47:29.481 --> 01:47:32.917
...to remove trade tariffs
on imported African rice...


01:47:33.084 --> 01:47:37.714
...with 582 members of the 736-seat body
voting to ratify the measure.


01:47:44.562 --> 01:47:48.658
Hey. Now you're free
to do whatever you want.


01:47:50.935 --> 01:47:53.028
Claudia Marie Taylor.


01:47:53.738 --> 01:47:56.400
- I like it.
- It suits you.


01:47:57.142 --> 01:47:58.507
Who are you?


01:47:58.676 --> 01:48:01.372
Henry. Henry Taylor.


01:48:01.546 --> 01:48:04.276
Ahh. Nice to meet you, Mr. Taylor.


01:48:04.449 --> 01:48:05.848
Nice to meet you.
